###### What is the issue?
All locale imports are statically imported, leading to unnecessary bundle size increase even when locales aren't used.


###### Why this matters
This approach loads all locale data into the bundle regardless of which locales are actually needed by the application, impacting initial load performance.

###### Suggested change ∙ *Feature Preview*
Implement dynamic imports for locales based on the user's selected language:
```typescript
async function loadLocale(locale: string) {
  await import(`dayjs/locale/${locale}`);
  dayjs.locale(locale);
}
```


